 #:seon.task{:name "build-artifact-is-a-second-indexing-path"
             :intent "`seon.fn/build-artifact` is a second indexing path beside the production one. It analyzes with no cache root (`seon.fn.analyzer/analyze` turns the cache off outside the checkout, analyzer.clj:818-822) and takes a hand-written first-party list, while the production path `seon.fn/program-entities` and analyzed-artifacts read the checkout cache and derive first-party from the database's entities. It has no src caller. Its test callers (fn_test ~881, 2071, 2080, 2132, 2431, 2843; program_test 1348; reset_edges_test 188; adoption_entities_test 15; edit_test 261; test/runner_test 163) mostly pass an empty first-party list and carry the same latent 'no analysis of seon.db' refusal since a9449b7c3. Delete it and convert its callers to `seon.fn/program-entities` in the same commit. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-3-2026-09-27.md`."}
