 #:seon.task{:name "the-outside-caller-publication-test-analyzes-the-whole-checkout"
             :intent "`seon.reset-edges-test/source-publication-refuses-an-outside-caller-and-keeps-its-head` is red on HEAD 606110768 under both evaluators. Compiled (`bin/seon check --at HEAD`, run 0641b8bb4778): `seon.fn/unresolved-macro-refusal` refuses `reset.publication.target` (clj-kondo holds no analysis of the fixture namespace) and the body takes 12.5 s against its 5 s bound. Interpreted (agent branch interp-reds-b): `seon.test-support/source-manifest` is a fresh SCI atom, so `seon.fn/build-manifest` analyzes every source root (13.8 s) and throws the NullPointerException of `seon.fn/a-finding-without-a-row-throws-in-lint-entities`. Done when the test declares its two fixture files to `seon.fn/build-artifact` with their dependency analysis and runs under its bound on both evaluators. See `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-13/interpreted-reds.md`."}
